-- isoleucine, the third case: two stereocentres rather than one, and a splitting at a methylene rather
-- than at a pair of methyls. The two methyls are not exchangeable even in the bond graph -- one hangs on
-- the beta carbon, the other on the end of the ethyl -- so the graph already separates them. What the
-- graph identifies and the configured molecule separates is the pair of hydrogens on the gamma
-- methylene, whose carbon neighbours the beta stereocentre.
data Ile = il-c1 | il-o1 | il-o2 | il-ho | il-ca | il-ha | il-n | il-hn1 | il-hn2 | il-cb | il-hb | il-cg1 | il-g11 | il-g12 | il-cd1 | il-d11 | il-d12 | il-d13 | il-cg2 | il-g21 | il-g22 | il-g23
